{"name":"Indigo Bunting","hex":"#006ca9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indigo bunting","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blue bunting of North America (Passerina cyanea)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indigo_bunting"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indigo bunting","blocks":[{"text":"The indigo bunting is a small seed-eating bird in the cardinal family, Cardinalidae. It is migratory, ranging from southern Canada to northern Florida during the breeding season, and from southern Florida to northern South America during the winter. It often migrates by night, using the stars to navigate. Its habitat is farmland, brush areas, and open woodland. The indigo bunting is closely related to the lazuli bunting and interbreeds with the species where their ranges overlap."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Indigo_Bunting_by_Dan_Pancamo_4.jpg/330px-Indigo_Bunting_by_Dan_Pancamo_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigo_bunting","wikidata":"Q1049642"},{"title":"Indigo","blocks":[{"text":"Indigo is a term used for a number of hues in the region of blue. The word comes from the ancient dye of the same name. The term \"indigo\" can refer to the color of the dye, various colors of fabric dyed with indigo dye, a spectral color, one of the seven colors of the rainbow as described by Sir Isaac Newton, or a region on the color wheel, and can include various shades of blue, ultramarine, and green-blue. Since the web era, the term has also been used for various purple and violet hues identified as \"indigo\", based on use of the term \"indigo\" in HTML web page specifications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Indian_indigo_dye_lump.jpg/330px-Indian_indigo_dye_lump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigo","wikidata":"Q5967009"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Indigo_Bunting_Female_by_Dan_Pancamo_1.jpg/500px-Indigo_Bunting_Female_by_Dan_Pancamo_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Indigo_Bunting_Female_by_Dan_Pancamo_1.jpg/1280px-Indigo_Bunting_Female_by_Dan_Pancamo_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Indigo_Bunting_Female_by_Dan_Pancamo_1.jpg/500px-Indigo_Bunting_Female_by_Dan_Pancamo_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndigo_Bunting_Female_by_Dan_Pancamo_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Passerina_cyaneaAAP086CA.jpg/500px-Passerina_cyaneaAAP086CA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Passerina_cyaneaAAP086CA.jpg/500px-Passerina_cyaneaAAP086CA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of male and female indigo bunting between 1910 and 1914.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APasserina_cyaneaAAP086CA.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Indigo_bunting_at_Smith_Oaks_Sanctuary%2C_High_Island.jpg/500px-Indigo_bunting_at_Smith_Oaks_Sanctuary%2C_High_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Indigo_bunting_at_Smith_Oaks_Sanctuary%2C_High_Island.jpg/1280px-Indigo_bunting_at_Smith_Oaks_Sanctuary%2C_High_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Indigo_bunting_at_Smith_Oaks_Sanctuary%2C_High_Island.jpg